body:
I think it would be extremely beneficial to be able to isolate section off HTML that ignore all CSS unless explicitly targeted. With modern apps having a lot of content being injected from 3rd parties it becomes very difficult to write defensive styles that are not unintentionally overwritten.

I have personally run into issues with a plugin that injects a specific type of search engine into a website, and having to fend of styling from over-aggressive themes and other plugins that may be installed. But I can see this also being beneficial for ads, and and other third party components that rely on styling to perform correctly.

The idea would be that the third party content, component, etc. would wrap itself in a `<realm>` tag to isolate it as an independently styled realm on the page. (I came up with realm but any name will do.) The realm tag would require an id attribute and must be targeted for CSS purposes using realm#id for any selector to match any of it's contents. The id would be required in the selector to prevent from accidentally applying styles to multiple realms. Then the author of the 3rd party content can can safely write their own styles using `realm#unique-id { /* styles */ }`. And not have other styles override them.

```html
<span>bar</span>

<realm id="foo-plugin">
    <span>foo</span>
</realm>
```

```css
span {
  color: red; /* would not match realm#foo span */
}

realm span {
  color: purple; /* would not match realm#foo span */
}

realm#foo span {
  color: green; /* would match */
}

span {
  color: yellow !important; /* would not match realm#foo span /*
}
```

This would still allow the user who is adding to 3rd party content to override styles, they would just need to specify the realm directly.

```css
a, realm#foo a, realm#other a {
  text-decoration: none;
}
```

Only the closest parent would need to be specified to match the selector:

```html
<realm id="third-party">
    <realm id="fourth-party">
        <span>foo</span>
    </realm>
</realm>
```

```css
realm#fourth-party span {
  background: red; /* would still match without specifying outer realm */
}
```
